hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17736","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us, al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu Nadra, that a man among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Abu Abdullah was visited by his companions while he was weeping. They said to him: What makes you weep. Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not say to you: Trim of your mustache, then keep it until you meet me. He said: Yes, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, Almighty and Majestic, grasped a handful with His right, and another with the other hand, and said: This is for this, and this is for this, and I do not care. So I do not know in which of the two handfuls I am."
"17737","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us who said: Said al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu Nadra who said: A man among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill, and his companions visited him to console him, and he wept. It was said to him: What makes you weep, O Abu Abdullah. Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not say to you: Trim of your mustache, then keep it until you meet me. He said: Yes, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, Almighty and Majestic, grasped a handful with His right and said: This is for this, and I do not care. And He grasped another handful with His other hand, Majestic and Exalted, and said: This is for this, and I do not care. So I do not know in which of the two handfuls I am."
